From c0e536b864e4851e3641699fc444192f7d4d9028 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: daveey <daveey@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 11 Nov 2026 06:06:34 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] [daveey] fix(auth): disabled accounts are refused on the
 singleton, aux, env-token and bound-session paths

Review of the disable feature found paths that hand out a token without pool selection:
- runtime_provider._resolve_oauth_runtime (Codex/xAI auth.json singleton) now raises AuthError
  when the singleton token is a disabled pool row's;
- auxiliary_client._read_codex_singleton_token drops it;
- anthropic _available_anthropic_token drops it for every caller, model or not;
- a Codex/xAI session bound to a row that gets disabled moves to an enabled row before its next
  request (rebind_off_disabled in _create_request_openai_client), AuthError if none is left;
- an Anthropic session pinned to a row that is disabled with no enabled row left raises
  AuthError instead of keeping the old token (reviewer repro);
- try_refresh_current/try_refresh_matching never refresh a disabled row; acquire_lease(id) of a
  disabled row leases another;
- the cache stamp includes st_ino (same size+mtime atomic replace was missed).
token_disabled costs nothing (no pool load) while nothing is disabled.

Proof: tests/agent/test_credential_pool_disabled_paths.py, 7 RED with the hooks reverted, all
GREEN; 163 pool/anthropic/routing/lifecycle/aux/auth/runtime_provider files: 1813 passed.
